---
/**
 * Where a new member lands. This is the Complete URL on the PayPal
 * membership button:
 *
 *   https://friendsofthelatimerhouse.org/thank-you/membership/
 *
 * It exists rather than reusing /thank-you/gift/ because that page is
 * wrong here twice over. It opens "Thank you. That goes into the house",
 * which is a gift, and it states that no goods or services were provided
 * in exchange, which is a claim about a gift with nothing attached.
 * Membership carries something: members hear first about workdays, open
 * houses and talks. That is a benefit, and benefits change what an
 * acknowledgment has to say.
 *
 * THE DEDUCTIBILITY STATEMENT, and the condition it rests on. Carried
 * here to match the gift pages, on the board's instruction, and it holds
 * for a specific reason worth writing down: the only thing members
 * receive is advance notice of workdays, open houses and talks that are
 * free and open to the public anyway. Notice of a free event is not a
 * good or a service with a value to subtract, so nothing reduces the
 * deduction and the acknowledgment can say so.
 *
 * THAT STOPS BEING TRUE the day membership carries something of value: a
 * members only event with refreshments, a tour nobody else gets, a mug, a
 * book, discounted admission to anything. At that point the quid pro quo
 * rules apply, the acknowledgment has to state the value of what was
 * received, and both this page and Give section 05 have to change. If the
 * board adds a member benefit, this comment is the thing to come back to.
 *
 * THE MEMBERSHIP YEAR. A year from the day you join, on every page that
 * mentions it. It used to say the calendar year, January through December,
 * which was written before the button existed and stopped being true the
 * moment it did: a PayPal yearly subscription renews on the anniversary of
 * the payment, so somebody joining in November renews in November. The
 * site was promising one thing and the payment was doing another, and the
 * first member to join outside January would have found out first.
 *
 * Three places say it now, and they have to keep agreeing: here, the
 * membership section of Get Involved, and the pointer on Give.
 *
 * noindex.
 */
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../../../components/PageHero.astro";
import NewsletterBand from "../../../components/NewsletterBand.astro";
import { org, mailingLine } from "../../../site.config";
---

<Base
  title="Welcome to the Friends"
  description="You are a member of the Friends of the Latimer House."
  noindex
>
  <PageHero
    crumbs={[{ label: "Thank You" }, { label: "Membership" }]}
    headline="You are one of the Friends."
    lead="Thank you for joining. Membership is the steadiest money this house gets, and it is what lets the board plan further ahead than one season at a time."
    image="/img/give-hero"
    imageAlt="The Latimer House."
    scrim={[0.94, 0.86, 0.72]}
  />
  <div class="torn-edge" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <section class="band band--parchment">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="ty">
        <div class="ty__col" data-aos="fade-up">
          <p class="eyebrow">Your membership</p>
          <div class="stack measure ty__body">
            <p>
              Your membership runs a year from today. The acknowledgment
              follows separately in writing, and PayPal has already emailed you
              a record of the transaction.
            </p>
            <p>
              {org.legalName}. EIN {org.ein}, a 501(c)(3) public charity.
              Contributions are deductible to the extent allowed by law, and a
              membership of two hundred fifty dollars or more carries the
              written acknowledgment the Internal Revenue Service requires,
              stating that no goods or services were provided in exchange. Our
              mailing address is {mailingLine}.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ty__col" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="150">
          <p class="eyebrow">What members get</p>
          <div class="stack measure ty__body">
            <p>
              Members hear first about workdays, open houses and talks. First
              means before it is announced anywhere else, and the way we reach
              you is the list at the foot of this page, so it is worth a moment
              if you are not on it yet.
            </p>
            <p class="ty__actions">
              <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/the-restoration/">
                See the work
                <span class="btn__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="foot" data-aos="fade-up">
        If something looks wrong, write to
        <a href={`mailto:${org.email}`}>{org.email}</a> and a board member will
        answer. The board is unpaid and there is no staff, so the person who
        replies is the person doing the work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NewsletterBand
    eyebrow="How we reach you"
    heading="This is where first comes from."
    body="Workdays, open houses and talks go out here before they go anywhere else. Not much other mail, and one click to leave."
    cta="Sign me up"
  />
</Base>

<style>
  .band { padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 2.25rem + 5vw, 6rem); }

  .ty {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 21rem), 1fr));
    gap: clamp(2rem, 1.25rem + 3vw, 4rem);
  }

  .ty__body { margin-block-start: 1rem; }
  .ty__body p { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .ty__body p a:not(.btn) {
    color: var(--forest-900);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .ty__body p a:not(.btn):hover { color: var(--hewn-600); }
  .ty__actions { margin-block-start: 1.75rem; }

  .foot {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-block-start: clamp(2.5rem, 1.75rem + 3vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-block-start: clamp(1.5rem, 1.25rem + 1vw, 2rem);
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted, var(--charcoal-600));
  }
  .foot a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .foot a:hover { color: var(--hewn-600); }
</style>
